1
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:05,858
This video shows you how to run the smeltr leader on Kubernetes,

2
00:00:05,858 --> 00:00:08,670
reach it through an Ingress, and sign in.

3
00:00:08,720 --> 00:00:10,094
Here's the cluster.

4
00:00:10,094 --> 00:00:12,068
It has three nodes.

5
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:18,353
It has a default storage class, which gives the leader its volumes.

6
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:23,191
Put the certificate for the leader's name in the cluster, as a TLS secret.

7
00:00:23,191 --> 00:00:25,528
The Ingress serves it later.

8
00:00:26,120 --> 00:00:27,764
Next, the leader's image.

9
00:00:27,764 --> 00:00:30,986
Copy the first commands from the container guide.

10
00:00:30,986 --> 00:00:34,348
They pull the release and read its digest.

11
00:00:40,240 --> 00:00:41,744
Then copy the checks.

12
00:00:41,744 --> 00:00:46,714
They pass only if smeltr's release workflow built this image.

13
00:00:56,400 --> 00:01:01,303
Save the verified digest in a file, to read into the manifest.

14
00:01:07,160 --> 00:01:13,877
Open a new file, smeltr-leader.yaml, and paste in the leader's manifest from the guide.

15
00:01:19,480 --> 00:01:20,966
It has three parts.

16
00:01:20,966 --> 00:01:24,070
A config map holds smeltr's settings.

17
00:01:24,120 --> 00:01:26,818
The leader listens on port 4000.

18
00:01:26,818 --> 00:01:32,070
The pod runs as an ordinary user, which can't open port 443.

19
00:01:32,120 --> 00:01:35,318
Change the public origin to your leader's address.

20
00:01:35,318 --> 00:01:37,830
It's the address your browser opens.

21
00:01:37,880 --> 00:01:43,470
Its own TLS is off, because the Ingress serves HTTPS in front of it.

22
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:48,444
A service gives the leader an address inside the cluster, on port 4000.

23
00:01:48,444 --> 00:01:51,510
Only the Ingress reaches it from outside.

24
00:01:51,560 --> 00:01:57,390
A stateful set runs the leader: one pod, which keeps its volumes when it restarts.

25
00:01:57,440 --> 00:01:59,826
Name the image by its digest.

26
00:01:59,826 --> 00:02:05,502
Delete the placeholder, and read in digest.txt with nano's Read File.

27
00:02:05,502 --> 00:02:08,135
A tag can move to a newer image.

28
00:02:08,135 --> 00:02:09,550
A digest can't.

29
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:13,281
These settings meet Kubernetes' restricted security standard.

30
00:02:13,281 --> 00:02:14,910
Leave them as they are.

31
00:02:14,960 --> 00:02:19,407
The leader keeps its data and its secrets key in two volumes.

32
00:02:19,407 --> 00:02:21,350
Back them up as one set.

33
00:02:21,400 --> 00:02:23,964
Size the data volume for your data.

34
00:02:23,964 --> 00:02:25,430
Here, ten gigabytes.

35
00:02:25,430 --> 00:02:30,030
The secrets volume holds one key, so one gigabyte is plenty.

36
00:02:30,080 --> 00:02:31,990
Save the file.

37
00:02:32,040 --> 00:02:35,275
Apply it, and wait for the leader's pod.

38
00:02:44,160 --> 00:02:49,335
Now open smeltr-ingress.yaml, and paste in the guide's Ingress.

39
00:02:56,720 --> 00:03:01,609
Change both names to your leader's address, the same as the public origin.

40
00:03:06,960 --> 00:03:09,719
It serves the certificate from the secret you made,

41
00:03:09,719 --> 00:03:12,270
and sends requests to the leader's service.

42
00:03:12,320 --> 00:03:14,798
Save it, and apply it.

43
00:03:18,720 --> 00:03:22,798
On its first start, the leader creates an administrator,

44
00:03:22,798 --> 00:03:26,070
and prints a one-time password in its log.

45
00:03:26,120 --> 00:03:26,566
Copy it.

46
00:03:26,566 --> 00:03:29,390
The leader prints it only on this first start.

47
00:03:29,440 --> 00:03:31,319
Open the leader at its address.

48
00:03:31,319 --> 00:03:35,110
Your browser trusts the certificate, so there's no warning.

49
00:03:35,160 --> 00:03:39,325
Sign in as admin, with the one-time password.

50
00:03:39,760 --> 00:03:43,767
Choose your own password, then sign in again with it.

51
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:56,417
Status shows one worker group, with no workers yet.

52
00:03:57,840 --> 00:03:59,639
Check on learning.

53
00:03:59,839 --> 00:04:02,389
The leader's TLS is off.

54
00:04:02,389 --> 00:04:06,602
What serves HTTPS to your browser?

55
00:04:11,002 --> 00:04:15,467
The Ingress, with the certificate in its TLS secret.

56
00:04:16,367 --> 00:04:20,056
Next, you add workers that keep their identity.
